{
  "name": "Greater Divine Intervention",
  "type": "feat",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>You are able to call on even more powerful divine intervention. When you use your Divine Intervention feature, you can select cleric spells up to 8th level. Additionally, you can select Wish when you select a spell. If you do so, you can't use Divine Intervention again until you finish 2d4 Long Rests. When you cast Wish with this feature, you are Immune to the stress caused by using Wish to do something other than casting a spell, other than the chance to lose the ability to cast the spell again.</p>",
